<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Maven's build cache (org.apache.maven.extensions:maven-build-cache-extension), loaded for every Maven
  invocation in this repository.

  WHY THE CACHE STAYS ON, INCLUDING FOR THE GATE. The recorded gate is `clean package` with
  `-Dmaven.compiler.useIncrementalCompilation=false`, because F-47 found the gate satisfiable by a previous
  revision's class files. A build cache is the same class of hazard — a cache hit could answer with outputs from an
  earlier revision — and the answer taken on 2026-10-03 was **not** to disable it: `scripts/lib/gate.js` keeps it on
  and says so in as many words. What makes that safe is that the cache checksums a module together with everything it
  reads, so a changed module cannot be answered from an earlier revision's outputs.

  (This paragraph claimed the opposite until 2026-10-06 — that the gate passed `-Dmaven.build.cache.enabled=false`
  and that `GateContractTest` asserted it — which was never true of the code. A reassuring sentence about a safety
  property is worse than no sentence, so it is corrected rather than deleted. AGENTS.md 2 states the rule: the cache
  is never turned off.)

  ANYTHING A BUILD DEPENDS ON THAT MAVEN CANNOT SEE must be added to this cache's inputs, which is what
  `.mvn/maven-build-cache-config.xml`'s `input/global/includes` and its per-module `input/project` are for. A path
  that is not hashed is a cache entry that silently answers for a change it never saw.

  The cache lives in the user's Maven repository (`~/.m2/build-cache`), not in the workspace: it is a fact about
  one machine, it survives `mvn clean`, and deleting it is always safe.
-->
<extensions xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/EXTENSIONS/1.0.0"
            xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
            xsi:schemaLocation="http://maven.apache.org/EXTENSIONS/1.0.0 https://maven.apache.org/xsd/core-extensions-1.0.0.xsd">
    <extension>
        <groupId>org.apache.maven.extensions</groupId>
        <artifactId>maven-build-cache-extension</artifactId>
        <version>1.2.0</version>
    </extension>
</extensions>
